From: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:28:06 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] mm/damon/core: do not update stat for core filter rejecting
 region

damos_apply_scheme() update stats for regions that were unable to apply
the scheme due to the quota.  Those are counted as tried and failed.  It
doesn't update stats for regions that were rejected by DAMOS core
filters.  Those are counted as not tried at all.

However, the DAMOS quota-driven failure is handled before DAMOS core
filter.  As a result, regions that would be rejected by the core filter
can be accounted as tried and failed.  As a result, users could show
confusing stat changes.

Fix by handling core filters before quotas.

The user impact is not critical.  No crash or leak happens.  Only the
DAMOS stat could occasionally move in an unexpected way.

Fixes: ab9bda001b68 ("mm/damon/core: introduce address range type damos filter")
Cc: <stable@vger.kernel.org> # 6.6.x
closes: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-9c51890e-a25c-4534-afab-ef33f22a9557
Signed-off-by: SJ Park <sj@kernel.org>
---
 mm/damon/core.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mm/damon/core.c b/mm/damon/core.c
index acaf8b892cf7..de439f7f27e6 100644
--- a/mm/damon/core.c
+++ b/mm/damon/core.c
@@ -2895,6 +2895,8 @@ static void damos_apply_scheme(struct damon_ctx *c, struct damon_target *t,
 	}
 
 	if (c->ops.apply_scheme) {
+		if (damos_core_filter_out(c, t, r, s))
+			return;
 		if (damos_quota_is_set(quota) &&
 				quota->charged_sz + sz > quota->esz) {
 			sz = ALIGN_DOWN(quota->esz - quota->charged_sz,
@@ -2904,8 +2906,6 @@ static void damos_apply_scheme(struct damon_ctx *c, struct damon_target *t,
 			if (damon_split_region_at(c, t, r, sz))
 				goto update_stat;
 		}
-		if (damos_core_filter_out(c, t, r, s))
-			return;
 		sz = damon_sz_region(r);
 		ktime_get_coarse_ts64(&begin);
 		trace_damos_before_apply(cidx, sidx, tidx, r, nr_accesses,
-- 
2.47.3

